<h1>Methodology</h1>
<p>TradingAI is a deterministic, rules-based intraday decision aid for NIFTY, BANKNIFTY and INDIA VIX. It does not predict markets. It classifies structure and permits at most one qualified setup per instrument per day.</p>
<div class="flow"><b>Workflow:</b> Market → Structure → Positioning → Liquidity → Intent → Confirmation → Trade / Wait / No Trade → Risk → Outcome → Research</div>
<h2>1. Market data</h2>
<ul><li>Free intraday source (yfinance), 5-minute candles in Asia/Kolkata.</li>
<li>Only <b>completed</b> candles are used: at time T, the latest usable candle is <code>floor_5m(T − 5 min)</code>. The forming candle never triggers decisions.</li>
<li>Quotes older than the freshness threshold are labelled <b>STALE</b> and never presented as live.</li></ul>
<h2>2. CPR &amp; levels (previous session only)</h2>
<ul><li>Pivot <code>(H+L+C)/3</code>, BC <code>(H+L)/2</code>, TC <code>2·Pivot − BC</code>; width <code>(TC−BC)/Pivot</code> → NARROW (&lt;0.15%), NORMAL, WIDE (&gt;0.30%).</li>
<li>Floor pivots: R1 <code>2·P−L</code>, S1 <code>2·P−H</code>, R2 <code>P+range</code>, S2 <code>P−range</code>.</li>
<li>Computed strictly from the previous session's OHLC — never from the current or a future session.</li></ul>
<h2>3. Session &amp; freshness gates</h2>
<ul><li>PREMARKET (&lt;09:15), LIVE (09:15–15:30 with data), MARKET_CLOSED, WEEKEND, plus STALE / NO_DATA feed states (NSE holiday calendar encoded).</li>
<li>Candle integrity: rejects duplicates, out-of-order, future-dated and invalid-OHLC data instead of repairing it.</li></ul>
<h2>4. Scenarios &amp; confirmation</h2>
<ul><li>Scenario types: bullish/bearish continuation, range premium decay, breakout, breakout-failure reversal.</li>
<li>Matches progress WATCH → PARTIALLY_MATCHED → CONFIRMED / INVALIDATED. Only CONFIRMED scenarios can qualify.</li>
<li>Point-in-time rule: historical decisions see only scenarios known at that timestamp (no lookahead).</li></ul>
<h2>5. Strategy selection</h2>
<ul><li>Bullish → Bull Put/Call Spread by volatility; Bearish → Bear Call/Put Spread; Neutral → Iron Condor. Unavailable options data → NO_TRADE.</li>
<li>Live qualification path: entry ≈ 0.5% below signal price; stop 1%; target 2%; reward:risk ≥ 1.5 and risk ≤ 2% or the setup is rejected.</li>
<li>CPR paper/backtest path (Backtest and Paper pages): first trigger per session, entry at next open in [09:20,15:10), 0.5% stop / 2% target at subsequent opens (stop first), flat 15:10 open; weekly-gated variant shown by default. See the Backtest page as canonical.</li></ul>
<h2>6. One trade per day</h2>
<ul><li>Maximum one qualified trade per instrument per day, enforced by persistent locks (race-safe across workers). Repeats report <code>DAILY_TRADE_LIMIT_REACHED</code>.</li></ul>
<h2>7. Paper trading &amp; backtests</h2>
<ul><li>Two paths exist: the live-qualification path above, and the CPR paper path (opens execution) shown on the Backtest and Paper pages. Their numbers differ by construction — same signals, different entry/exit rules.</li>
<li>Paper trades are tracked to stop/target exits — no broker connection exists. Backtests replay stored 5-minute sessions; paper ledgers are frozen snapshots regenerated by the daily job (live spreads refresh every 60s).</li></ul>
<h2>8. What the site will not claim</h2>
<ul><li>No win-rate, accuracy or profitability statements appear unless backed by the validated historical record shown on the Backtest page. Absence of data is shown as such — never filled in.</li></ul>
